{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 returned 0xff (idle) with divider 64, indicating ser_tx never left idle. Root cause is the TX divider path in the excerpt: `if (reg_div_we) send_dummy <= 1;` starts a 15-bit dummy idle frame that blocks the immediate `reg_dat_we` byte so it is dropped, and the TX bit timer uses `(cfg_divider >> 4)` instead of `cfg_divider` making TX 16x too fast.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -109,6 +109,4 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
-		if (reg_div_we)
-			send_dummy <= 1;
 		send_divcnt <= send_divcnt + 1;
 		if (!resetn) begin
 			send_pattern <= ~0;
@@ -127,7 +125,7 @@
 			send_bitcnt <= 10;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end

